- **W2 same-day asymmetry survives.** It does not shrink when realized variance is computed on 15, 30, or 60-minute grids, so the "bid bounce" artifact story is broken. A persistent spread-widening artifact remains possible and needs ask-side data.
- **W3 gold null is weakened** only by the same downtrend subsets as W1. All other regime cuts stay under |t| 2.4.
- **W4 wall width** survives in-sample at half size after year dummies, but is broken out-of-sample (t +0.7). The out-of-sample "thinner" effect is year composition from the 2024-25 rally.

**Recommendation recorded for the research lane.** Rewrite the proposed prospective cell as one-sided (downtrend-state γ below zero, uptrend γ indistinguishable from zero), since the symmetric interaction passes automatically whenever the downside half holds.

