**Target** — cycle43's only positive carry-forward: gold's non-OPEX Friday 15:30→16:00 ET direction "continuing" into Monday 10:00. External 2021-26H1 β +1.843 (HC1 t 2.70, n 208), sign strategy +20.8 bp/day (t 3.15), recent +37.2 (t 3.05), in-sample null. Research branch (d) would have annotated c36's prospective Friday→Monday cell with it.

**Verdict: broken as framed — survived as a statistical fact.** 10 break rules pre-registered; 2 landed.

Eight attacks failed (the number is robust): exact replication; outlier removal (top-3 contributors = only 20% of S, t stays 2.68); drift decomposition (long-gold carry explains **0%**); rank tests (Spearman p 0.017, Wilcoxon p 0.006); weekday-specificity (other four weekdays all null, Friday interaction t 2.86); sign-randomization p 0.0015; cost (net t 2.54 at 2× cost + swap; breaks only above 9.9 bp); boundary re-splits 2019/21/22/23 all preserve the structure and odd/even years are symmetric; ±5-min grid shifts; shared-endpoint removal. Post-hoc, vol-normalization also failed to kill it (+0.212σ, t 2.87) — so it isn't just bp scaling with gold's vol.

Two landed, and three mechanism tests killed the *story*:
- **Multiple testing (decisive)**: Bonferroni 0.074 (family 45) / 0.118 (72). Structurally, β_ctrl/S_ctrl were never hypotheses — they're the **control arm** of a test about OPEX days.
