**I did not break c45's direction — I broke its entitlement to the conclusion.** The honest statement is "probably right, not established here." I also retracted my own stronger reading: ANN_NJ vs ANN_J is null at event level (+0.210, t 0.77, p 0.26), so "no jump is better" is unsupported — only "a jump isn't required." My BREAK-A was written as a one-sided threshold; written as a symmetric contrast it would have misfired, so my rule-writing held the conclusion. The c4 single-frozen-scan confound stays unresolved.

